(IIT Kharagpur ML Security Hackathon - Problem 1) Tj
T*
(Clean-Only HPC Backdoor Anomaly Detection) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Objective) Tj
T*
(Detect inference traces that differ from benign HPC behavior, with no) Tj
T*
(backdoor traces available during training. The supplied file has 800 clean) Tj
T*
(inferences and three hardware performance counters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Data preparation) Tj
T*
(Features: cycles, cache-references, LLC-loads. The unnamed sequential) Tj
T*
(column is a row index and is dropped. Features are log\(cycles\),) Tj
T*
(log\(cache-references/cycles\), and log\(LLC-loads/cache-references\).) Tj
T*
(Cache references and LLC loads have approximately 0.92 Pearson correlation) Tj
T*
(in the supplied clean traces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proposed detector) Tj
T*
(A Gaussian mixture density is fitted to the joint transformed HPC vector.) Tj
T*
(BIC selects the mixture size on the fitting split. The anomaly score is) Tj
T*
(negative log likelihood. A separate clean calibration split sets the) Tj
T*
(threshold at the configured 95th percentile. The artifact saves scaler,) Tj
T*
(model, feature names, and threshold.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Evaluation design) Tj
T*
(Twenty-five deterministic clean-only splits: 60% fit, 20% calibration,) Tj
T*
(20% held-out clean evaluation. Baselines: \(1\) per-counter GMM proxy using) Tj
T*
(the maximum standardized marginal negative log likelihood, and \(2\) joint) Tj
T*
(GMM on log raw counter values. The proposed work-conditioned feature GMM) Tj
T*
(is compared using identical splits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clean-only results: mean held-out FPR +/- standard deviation) Tj
T*
(Per-counter GMM proxy: 5.33% +/- 2.21%) Tj
T*
(Joint raw-log GMM: 4.60% +/- 1.78%) Tj
T*
(Work-conditioned feature GMM: 4.75% +/- 1.81%) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Interpretation and limits) Tj
T*
(These results measure clean false alarms only. Small FPR differences do) Tj
T*
(not demonstrate superior backdoor detection. No attack examples were) Tj
T*
(provided, so TPR, attack FPR, F1, and AUROC cannot be calculated. Triggered) Tj
T*
(proxy runs, if collected, must be reported as separate evaluation.) Tj
T*
(Calibration assumes future clean traces are comparable to calibration) Tj
T*
(traces; it does not guarantee the same FPR under distribution shift.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Related work) Tj
T*
(Alam, Wang, Maniatakos, DATE 2024, Detecting Backdoor Attacks in Black-Box) Tj
T*
(Neural Networks through Hardware Performance Counters.) Tj
T*
(https://past.date-conference.com/proceedings-archive/2024/DATA/1142_pdf_upload.pdf) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reproduction commands) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
